<% title "Guardian Agreement" %>

<h1 class="heading">Guardian Agreement</h1>
<p class="muted">
  Version <%= @agreement_version %>.
  This is the agreement a parent or legal guardian accepts when they take
  responsibility for a teen's Fuime account.
</p>

<%= render "application/callout", type: "info", title: "Read this before you accept an invite" do %>
  <p class="m0">
    If your teen has invited you to be their guardian, this is the text you
    will be agreeing to. It is published here so you can read it before
    clicking anything in an email. When you accept, Fuime records the date and
    time, your IP address, your browser, and the version above — so there is a
    permanent record of exactly what you agreed to.
  </p>
<% end %>

<% if @agreement_partial.present? %>
  <%# Fuime: the same versioned partial the signing flow renders. Rendering the
      real thing — rather than a copy maintained alongside it — is what stops
      the published agreement drifting from the binding one. The named minor is
      a stand-in here; see StaticPagesController#guardian_agreement. %>
  <%= render @agreement_partial, minor: @specimen_minor, guardian: nil %>
<% else %>
  <p>
    We could not load the agreement text. Please email
    <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %> and we will send it to you.
  </p>
<% end %>

<hr>

<h2>Withdrawing consent</h2>
<p>
  You can withdraw consent at any time by emailing
  <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %>. When you do, the teen can no longer
  operate a business on Fuime. You do not have to give a reason.
</p>

<h2>Questions</h2>
<p>
  If anything here is unclear, email <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %> before
  you accept. We would much rather answer a question than have you agree to
  something you are unsure about.
</p>

<p class="muted">
  See also our <%= link_to "Terms of Service", terms_path %> and
  <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path %>.
</p>
